{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Do this.</b> Meaning: this matter you do not need to do with permission, but the wagons you cannot make except with permission — and even permission from Yosef would not suffice; rather, it must be said that he is acting with Pharaoh's authorization. And this is what the verse means by saying <b>and you are commanded</b> etc., and likewise it says <b>and he gave them</b> etc. <b>wagons according to the mouth of Pharaoh</b>, and this was in accordance with the customs of Egypt." "<b>Further,</b> it intends by saying <b>do this</b>, that he was commanding them — not that he merely wished to do kindness with them, but that he desired the matter and said <b>do this.</b> And from HaShem the matter went forth, in order that our fathers would go down to Egypt."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:52.680239250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}